+## 2026-11-22: Evolved Elite Barbarians' Rage lasts 2 s (patch 0055)
+
+**GAMEPLAY-AFFECTING.** One number, from an official note.
+
+The official 8 September 2026 balance note reads "Elite Barbarians Evolution:
+Spear Range: 3.5-5 -> 3-4.5 tiles (-10%), Rage Duration: 2.5s -> 2s (-20%)".
+The registry already had the new band and the 26 August spear damage (220),
+but the Rage still lasted the August 2.5 s (25 ticks). It is 20 ticks now.
+
+Why this card was looked at: in the replay forensics the Elite Barbarians are
+the top source of the first excess damage against the Hog 2.6 side, and 257
+of 258 such events are the Evolution's deck slot (card 178), which in the
+"any" sample over-performs by +0.116 in win rate.
+
+What the traces of the standard answers showed (scratch `eb.py`), and what is
+NOT changed here because no published value decides it:
+
+- The published scalars of `AngryBarbarian` all match: Speed 90 (Fast, 2.0
+  tiles/s measured), hit speed 1.4 s, first hit 0.5 s after reaching range
+  (LoadTime 900), sight 6.0, range 1.2, deploy 1.0 s, 1341 hp, 384 damage.
+- The published table of release 15.535.13 has no record of the evolved form
+  (`AngryBarbarians_EV1` is `NotInUse`), so the spear is known only from the
+  three official notes (26 Aug, 8 Sep, 6 Oct 2026) and descriptions. The
+  engine's spear is an instant 220 on the nearest enemy ground troop 3-4.5
+  tiles away, checked every tick, with no wind-up and no flight. An Ice Spirit
+  (215 hp) is therefore always dead before it can jump (range 2.5), and each
+  Skeleton in the band is one spear. Whether the real spear has a wind-up or
+  flight long enough for the spirit to jump first, whether it is thrown at the
+  barbarian's own target only, and whether buildings and Crown Towers are
+  valid targets are all unpublished; the 6 Oct note ("Spear Attack Sight
+  Range: 4.5 -> 6 tiles ... will no longer ignore troops outside of their base
+  sight range while throwing their spears") suggests it is an attack of his
+  with its own sight, not a free periodic effect.
+- The pair deploys abreast (offsets +-0.5; published SummonRadius 700) but
+  walks in a column 0.8-1.0 tiles apart once it has crossed a bridge (166 of
+  234 pairs in the events), because `Board::getNextWaypoint` funnels every
+  crosser through the bridge's centre point, although the bridge is two tiles
+  wide. The second barbarian reaches a tower 0.8 s after the first.
+- No deploy stagger: the published `SummonDeployDelay` (100 ms per unit for
+  most multi-unit cards) is not modelled.
+- Collision radius 0.4 against the published 0.5.
+
+Test: `tests/core/test_cards_0015.cpp` `[patch0055]` (the registered evolved
+pair throws one spear each at a troop in the band and is enraged for exactly
+20 updates).
+
